## Expected vs. actual behavior

**Expected:** scsynth opens no supernova build, since each one has a scsynth version next to it.

**Actual (develop):** it opens all 26 core supernova builds, then closes them:

```
supernova builds opened by scsynth: 26
  GendynUGens_supernova.scx
  PanUGens_supernova.scx
  DiskIO_UGens_supernova.scx
  ...
```

**With the fix:**

```
supernova builds opened by scsynth: 0
```

Every third-party package that ships both builds (sc3-plugins, for example) adds its supernova builds to this list. With many extensions installed, these useless `dlopen` calls cost a few seconds at every scsynth boot. The fix removes that time, and the same scsynth plugins are still loaded.

## Problem

**File:** `server/scsynth/SC_Lib_Cintf.cpp`

`PlugIn_LoadDir()` (line 407) calls `PlugIn_Load()` on every `.scx` file (line 436). `PlugIn_Load()` (line 319) opens the file with `dlopen(filename, RTLD_NOW)` (line 371), and only then checks which server it was built for (line 384):

```cpp
void* serverCheckPtr = (void*)dlsym(handle, "server_type");
if (!checkServerVersion(serverCheckPtr, filename.c_str())) {
    dlclose(handle);
    return false;
}
```

Every supernova build is therefore mapped, symbol-bound, initialized and closed for nothing. On macOS, the cost of each `dlopen` also grows with the number of libraries already loaded.

## Possible Fix

**File to modify:** `server/scsynth/SC_Lib_Cintf.cpp`, 3 places (line numbers from develop 5d47207bb).

**1. Before line 82** (`void initMiscCommands();`): add a helper that recognizes a supernova build whose scsynth version (`Foo.scx` or `Foo_scsynth.scx`) is in the same folder.

```diff
@@ -79,6 +79,20 @@
 #    define LINUX_PLUGIN_WORKAROUND
 #endif

+// "Foo_supernova.scx" next to "Foo.scx" or "Foo_scsynth.scx" is the supernova build: PlugIn_Load would
+// dlopen it only to reject it, which is costly with many plugins.
+static bool isSupernovaTwinOfScsynthPlugin(const fs::path& file) {
+    static const std::string supernovaSuffix = "_supernova";
+    const std::string stem = file.stem().string();
+    if (stem.size() < supernovaSuffix.size()
+        || stem.compare(stem.size() - supernovaSuffix.size(), supernovaSuffix.size(), supernovaSuffix) != 0)
+        return false;
+    const std::string base = stem.substr(0, stem.size() - supernovaSuffix.size());
+    std::error_code ec;
+    return fs::exists(file.parent_path() / (base + SC_PLUGIN_EXT), ec)
+        || fs::exists(file.parent_path() / (base + "_scsynth" + SC_PLUGIN_EXT), ec);
+}
+
 void initMiscCommands();
 #ifdef LINUX_PLUGIN_WORKAROUND
 static bool PlugIn_LoadDir(const fs::path& dir, bool reportError, bool isTopLevel = true, bool foundScxFile = false);
```

